1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:03,612
CHAPTER 8 — THE PIGEON MAN

2
00:00:03,962 --> 00:00:14,269
In his final years he lived in New York hotels. He spent his nights feeding the pigeons. He said he loved one white pigeon like no other.

3
00:00:14,469 --> 00:00:23,546
Engineers awarded him their highest prize: the Edison Medal. According to his biographer, in the middle of the ceremony he vanished.

4
00:00:23,746 --> 00:00:27,515
They found him in a plaza, covered in pigeons.

5
00:00:27,715 --> 00:00:36,023
He died alone in his hotel room in 1943. He was eighty-six years old and had almost no money.

6
00:00:36,523 --> 00:00:48,831
Since 1960, his last name is a unit: the tesla. A hospital MRI scanner uses between 1.5 and 3. A fridge magnet, a few thousandths.

7
00:00:49,031 --> 00:00:54,646
And his induction motors keep spinning in factories, water pumps, and fans.

8
00:00:54,846 --> 00:01:00,385
While you watch this, the current in your home goes back and forth, pushed by his idea.

9
00:01:00,585 --> 00:01:07,892
The night he was born, the midwife said he would be a child of the storm. His mother said no: of light.

10
00:01:08,842 --> 00:01:10,535
They were both right.

11
00:01:11,485 --> 00:01:16,715
And now tell us in the comments: what story would you like to see in the next episode?
